 "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trusting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "inspiring confidence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We want to build a trusting work environment. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about company policies."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flexibility"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of being flexible; able to easily make changes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There may be some flexibility, but as a rule of thumb, you should arrive before 9:00 a.m."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the exception rather than the rule"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that occurs rarely; that is not very common"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As a rule of thumb, arriving after 9:00 should be the exception rather than the rule."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "t\u00eate-\u00e0-t\u00eate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a private conversation, often on a sensitive or personal topic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like to have a little t\u00eate-\u00e0-t\u00eate about some company policies. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "transition"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "change from one status or condition to another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My job is to make sure your transition into the role of editorial assistants goes as smoothly and seamlessly as possible."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le06ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Minimal Pairs and Consonant Clusters"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Minimal pairs are two words which sound the same, except for one sound. It is useful to practice saying minimal pairs to perfect your pronunciation of two sounds. <br/> Consonant clusters are a group of 2 or more consonants that are pronounced together in one sound. <br/><br/>  Let's look at minimal pairs comparing the sounds: sh and ch (consonant clusters) and th and t. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The sounds <span class=\"italic\">sh</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ch</span> are quite similar, except for the position of your lips and the length of the air flow.<br/> Compare the two sounds. Say them out loud: <span class=\"italic\">sh</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ch</span>.<br/><br/>  Now say these minimal pairs:<br/><br/>  share&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp    chair<br/> shoes&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp   choose<br/><br/>  The sounds <span class=\"italic\">th</span> and <span class=\"italic\">t</span> are both unvoiced sounds. They are quite different in terms of the position of your teeth tongue.<br/>  Compare the two sounds. Say them out loud: <span class=\"italic\">th</span> and <span class=\"italic\">t</span>.<br/><br/>  Now say these minimal pairs:<br/><br/>  tree&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp   three<br/> boat&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp  both<br/><br/>  Practice reading the following sentences from the text aloud. Focus on the pronunciation of the ch, sh, th and t sounds."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Three people will share this office. You have a lovely view of the tree outside. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Please, take this chair. We share furniture around here."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals to Express True and Possible: In my opinion, We should, Ought to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> to give your subjective opinion about whether you think something is possible or true. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I've fixed the toilet and it <span class=\"strong\">should</span> be working all right now.<br/> You <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> wear that blue suit - it suits you!</span><br/><br/>   It is more common to use should and ought to when you give your opinion about whether something is right nor not. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>    <span class=\"italic\">You really <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't</span> wear that - it is not flattering.<br/> There <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> be a larger table in here - we can't work on that!</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The counterpart of that means that you will ought to be very reliable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next, we should talk about establishing an appropriate work schedule."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You shouldn't spread gossip or accumulate absences."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose 3 very large corporations, such as Disney, Apple Computers, eBay, etc."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online. Find information about some policies in these companies. The policies can be related to hiring, marketing, attendance, etc."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 2 interesting policies for each company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a summary of the policies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss the policies. Say what you think is good or not good about each one. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about policies in different companies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a summary of policies in different companies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss my opinion of policies in different companies."}]}], "type": "sena"}